WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.416
Unless, until and without all use one method.

2
00:00:03.716 --> 00:00:05.444
Find the two complete ideas.

3
00:00:05.744 --> 00:00:07.472
Choose either one and negate it.

4
00:00:07.772 --> 00:00:10.652
That negated idea is the sufficient condition.

5
00:00:10.952 --> 00:00:12.829
Leave the other idea unchanged.

6
00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:15.049
The game is played unless it rains.

7
00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:16.864
Choose the idea it rains.

8
00:00:17.164 --> 00:00:21.644
Its negation is it does not rain, so if it does not rain, the game is played.

9
00:00:21.944 --> 00:00:24.504
Now choose the other idea, the game is played.

10
00:00:24.804 --> 00:00:29.519
Its negation is the game is not played, so if the game is not played, it rains.

11
00:00:29.819 --> 00:00:34.171
Both versions rule out the same situation: no rain and no game.

12
00:00:34.471 --> 00:00:36.497
They are contrapositives of each other.

13
00:00:36.797 --> 00:00:39.016
The rule also leaves some facts open.

14
00:00:39.316 --> 00:00:42.260
If it rains, we cannot tell whether the game is played.

15
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.568
If the game is played, we cannot tell whether it rains.

16
00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:49.815
You might expect rain to cancel the game, but this rule never says so.

17
00:00:50.115 --> 00:00:52.611
Sometimes an idea already contains not.

18
00:00:52.911 --> 00:00:56.089
The store does not open unless the manager arrives.

19
00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:59.739
Negate the store does not open, and you get the store opens.

20
00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:02.791
So if the store opens, the manager arrives.

21
00:01:03.091 --> 00:01:04.819
Find the two complete ideas.

22
00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:08.468
Choose one, negate it, and make it the sufficient condition.

23
00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:12.117
Keep the other unchanged, and read the rule back in English.
